{"name":"Bona Fide","hex":"#304471","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bona fide","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["In good faith; genuinely, sincerely."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["In good faith; sincere; without deception or ulterior motive.","Genuine; not counterfeit."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bona_fide"}],"entries":[{"title":"Good faith","blocks":[{"text":"In human interactions, good faith is a sincere intention to be fair, open, and honest, regardless of the outcome of the interaction. It is an important concept within law and business. The opposed concepts are bad faith, mala fides (duplicity) and perfidy (pretense)."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Good_faith"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/LMW_Dupondius_RIC_1210_R%C3%BCckseite_Bildarchiv_79628.jpg/500px-LMW_Dupondius_RIC_1210_R%C3%BCckseite_Bildarchiv_79628.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/LMW_Dupondius_RIC_1210_R%C3%BCckseite_Bildarchiv_79628.jpg/500px-LMW_Dupondius_RIC_1210_R%C3%BCckseite_Bildarchiv_79628.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Reverse of a dupondius issued under the emperor Vespasian depicting Fides Publica, the public trust, holding a patera as a symbol of religious fidelity and a cornucopia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALMW_Dupondius_RIC_1210_R%C3%BCckseite_Bildarchiv_79628.jpg"}],"sounds":{"bona fide":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/80/En-us-bona-fide_2.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/8/80/En-us-bona-fide_2.ogg/En-us-bona-fide_2.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.